A||||12||RZURCTN||Still have an EGR prob!!||||1||
Z||000000||RZURCTN||01-13-2000||02:35 PM||||OK. 84 2.5L. Replaced the EGR.  The old one was sticking open.  Now it runs fine at idle and at W.O.T.  In between, when the EGR is open, it stumbles really bad.  Could it be a bad O2 sensor?  Or is it something else?  It still runs fine when the EGR is unplugged!  TIA!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||ka4nkf||01-13-2000||08:28 PM||||I had a four cyl. that did the same thing. I did like you and replaced the EGR but did not help. The problem was it was getting too much egr and i could not figure out how to fix it. I even tried to make a valve to slow the vac down but never got it to work right. So i just unhooked the egr and it ran great, but i did have to burn premium gas, I hear lots of pros and cons on running one without egr but i never had any trouble for 40,000 miles until i sold it. I have a V-6 Now and have the EGR unhooked also ,runs like a dream but i dont have to use premium gas in it, and it does not ping. I hate EGR valves. Besides why do you want to put dirty exhaust gas with the good fuel. I live in Kentucky and we dont have emission laws so i guess i am lucky.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||01-14-2000||01:39 AM||||same  here in west virginia.....<P>just those damn expection stickers......   yet, kentucky doesnt have these either...  <P>u lucky man...<P>where u from in ky?   I am right on the border of ky... close to Phelps Ky if you have heard of that..<P>chris..||||reg||6
Z||000003||ka4nkf||01-14-2000||08:23 AM||||Chris i am in paducah, ky. It is halfway between posum trot and monkeys eyebrow. And that is the truth.||||reg||1
Z||000004||V6pack||01-14-2000||10:13 AM||||I picked up a V6 recently that had the symptoms you describe. The solenoid and valve were working correctly, but any mid thottle (1500 to 2500) rpm seemed to choke it up and the engine would stumble.<P>I had to pass Ca. smog, so after eliminating the O2 sensor and the cat as the culprits I was stuck. Couldn't pass the visual inspection unhooked either.<P>A mechanic friend gave me a sheet of metal gasket material.  He said to cut it the same size as the gasket under the EGR valve...duh, and put two or three small holes (end of a ink pen size in the metal gasket.<P>It worked well with two holes, it drew enough exhaust from the egr for me to pass the smog test and the visual inspection.<P>No more stumbles, no codes, runs fine.  I'd sure like to know the real cause but I was sure happy with this "shade tree" fix.<BR>V6pack<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||01-14-2000||10:49 AM||||V6Pack <BR>Thats good glad it worked. the problem that i find is it gets too much vac and this makes it run bad. i never thought about the gasket method but that sure sounds like a winner. put no more holes than you need to pass the smog test. I believe you have come up with the solution.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||V6pack||01-14-2000||11:41 AM||||Well kn4, I can't take any credit. I was just lucky this knarled old mech. was kind enough to share his "fix".<P>He is one of those old school guys that doesn't have much time for manuals or any of that scan tool ^*#&, as he puts it.<P>I was still bugged even when it ran great after the fix, because I had to know what the problem was.  He said, "What do you care? It runs don't it?"<P>Not a bad attitude sometimes, but I'd still like to know the "why". :-)<BR>V6pack<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000007||DRH||01-14-2000||02:42 PM||||Just a guess here... What about a small vacuum leak somewhere else??? With the EGR unplugged the ECM can compensate for the extra air???<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||RZURCTN||01-14-2000||05:27 PM||||Sounds like blocking the EGR off with the tin is doing the same thing as having it unplugged.  Even if you do poke a couple holes in it.  I agree with the philosphy of "if it ain't broke, don't fix it", but the whole problem is that it is broke!  If it was working right the EGR would be plugged in and it would run fine.  It's just one of those things that really bugs me.  I hate to be stumped by a problem like this.  And I hate to say this, but I don't run premium gas in anything!  Have you seen the price for that stuff lately?!?  As if regular weren't expensive enough!    <P>Still, if anyone can hazard a guess as to what is causing my problem, I'd love to hear it!  Thanks!||||reg||1
