Z||000011||RZURCTN||01-16-2000||11:25 PM||||I still haven't cured the timing problem.  Maybe I'll change distributors again.  But I'm not so sure that timing is what is causing or aiding my EGR problem.  Since the EGR system is non-electrical and not ECM controlled, I figure it has to be something more mundane.  Maybe an exhaust leak? Or an intake leak?  Or a bad vacuum line somewhere? Or......?????  Who knows!  All I know is that I haven't been able to figure it out.  <BR>  On the bright side, I haven't had any pinging while running it without the EGR. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||01-18-2000||03:30 AM||||just looked at this thread, and I've been haveing the same problems as you on my 84 duck, except mine only stumbles when it's cold.  When the duck warms up it nearly runs decent... my timing also jumps around when I try to set it.  Right now I'm pretty sure it's a vacuum leak somewhere, most likely the gasket under the TBI... ||||reg||1
